  "title": "US Supreme Court Revisits Mail-In Voting Restrictions in Midterm Elections",
  "summary": "The US Supreme Court renewed its appeal to allow restrictions on mail-in voting in November’s midterm elections, following a federal judge’s earlier decision to block new limits. The Trump administration seeks further legal action to address concerns over voter access.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The US Supreme Court renewed its appeal to allow restrictions on mail-in voting in November’s midterm elections.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A federal judge, David Carter, denied the Justice Department’s request to withhold disputed ballots pending citizenship checks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
