  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Judge rebuffs Trump DoJ’s bid to force California to set aside 20,000 ballots",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/28/federal-judge-trump-california-ballots",
      "description": "<p>Justice department had demanded state segregate and not count ballots from people it claimed were non-citizens</p><p>A federal judge <a href=\"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cacd.1043513/gov.uscourts.cacd.1043513.149.0.pdf\">declined to order</a> California election officials to segregate and not count ballots from people the Trump administration claimed were non-citizens, rebuffing a legally thin request from the justice department that appeared designed to cast doubt over the results of the midterms.</p><p>The ruling from US district judge David Carter, nominated to the federal bench by Bill Clinton, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/15/justice-department-sues-california-midterms\">comes about two weeks</a> after the justice department delivered a USB drive to election officials in Los Angeles and Sacramento that it said contained the names of 20,000 non-citizens on the state’s voter rolls. There are more than 23 million registered voters in California and non-citizen voting is <a href=\"https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/noncitizen-voting-vanishingly-rare\">extremely rare</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/28/federal-judge-trump-california-ballots\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-29T01:54:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "US judge rejects Trump admin's bid to block 20,000 California mail-in votes",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-judge-rejects-trump-admin-s-bid-to-block-20-000-california-mail-in-votes-126102900108_1.html",
      "description": "Judge David O. Carter denied the Justice Department's request to withhold disputed ballots pending citizenship checks, warning the move could disrupt the midterm elections",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T03:02:39"
